<title>GERMANY: Ford raises German prices average 1.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Ford raises German prices average 1.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COLOGNE, Germany 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German unit of U.S. carmaker Ford Motor Co said on Wednesday it has raised the prices of vehicles in its product range on average 1.9 percent.</p>
<p>Ford said the price increases, which include taxes and are based on delivery at the factory, take effect on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The carmaker gave the following information on new vehicle prices (prices are in marks):</p>
<p>    --Fiesta Focus (three-door)	     18,990</p>
<p>    --Escort Champ				24,200</p>
<p>    --Mondeo CLX 16V			    33,990</p>
<p>    --Probe 16V				   40,900</p>
<p>    --Galaxy CLX (2.0 liter engine)	 39,990</p>
<p>    --Galaxy CLX (2.3 liter engine)	 41,690</p>
<p>Ford said the price recommendations, which refer to entry models, were not binding on dealers.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
